WEBVTT

1
00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:30.600
Just ask for the floor, colleague. Please.

2
00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:36.240
I'm asking one more question, it concerns life on farmsteads.

3
00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:43.300
On a farmstead between Crvenka and Sivac, the spouses Dragica and Danilo Kaluđerski live without electricity in the 21st century.

4
00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:49.440
That is, for 20 years they have been waging a futile fight to have electricity brought to the farmstead.

5
00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:53.700
The farmstead isn't remote, it's located right by the regional road

6
00:00:53.700 --> 00:01:10.260
Novi Sad — Sombor, so it's not the kind of farmstead where electricity can't be brought.

7
00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:14.980
They simply turn to the local government in Kula, to "Elektrodistribucija" in Sombor, etc.

8
00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:25.360
So, that power line about 4 km long that needs to be run for the Kaluđerski farmstead to get electricity —

9
00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:34.060
not only they would connect to this line, which would indeed in a way be pointless,

10
00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:44.740
but about a hundred farmsteads and weekend houses around the Kaluđerski farmstead would connect to this line.

11
00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:52.160
That's why I ask you: has Serbia really forgotten the little people who spent their lives on farmsteads,

12
00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:56.400
and those who in their youth decided to live on farmsteads?

13
00:01:56.540 --> 00:02:05.020
Is it possible for this part of Vojvodina to get electricity, for which only one thing is needed — to connect to this line?

14
00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:11.370
The minister, Mr. Nedimović, has the floor, please.

15
00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:14.990
Thank you. I would just ask you to forward this initiative to me,

16
00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:19.910
I'll visit them, let them gather all the interested people,

17
00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:23.910
sit down with the municipality head from Kula, and we'll agree to get this solved.

18
00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:32.290
This is no big problem, there just need to be more users so that we know.

19
00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:37.350
Surveying people is no problem, thank you for that, I'll do everything so that we solve this.

20
00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:42.940
Bring Guli a chair, Danilo.

21
00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:49.080
They promise a change in the weather.

22
00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:49.660
When?

23
00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:51.180
From Sunday.

24
00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:54.720
It's gotten warmer now.

25
00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:02.340
I was at church before lunch, such a cold wind was blowing that really...

26
00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:07.340
And when did people start building weekend houses here and all that?

27
00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:11.300
Well, they started building weekend houses a very long time ago.

28
00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:12.320
When?

29
00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:15.240
A very long time ago, oh my.

30
00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:19.280
It's been 30 years since they started building weekend houses.

31
00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:21.020
And how many weekend houses are there now?

32
00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:22.860
In this part?

33
00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:26.200
Well, 30, if not more.

34
00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:31.720
If you join this part and that part — more than 30 weekend houses.

35
00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:37.780
Does anyone live here?

36
00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:38.800
No.

37
00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:42.760
There's a house here built for more than 10,000 euros.

38
00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:47.320
There's a two-story house, no electricity, the man gave up, didn't build any further.

39
00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:49.560
And which municipality does your farmstead belong to?

40
00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:50.040
To Sivac.

41
00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:54.620
180 meters — on Sivac land, and it belongs to Sivac.

42
00:04:56.080 --> 00:05:01.040
And is Crvenka far, is the plant far, this sugar factory and the "Jaffa" factory?

43
00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:03.900
The village is 2 kilometers from the farmstead.

44
00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:05.380
Crvenka.

45
00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:05.760
And the center — is 3.

46
00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:11.500
So in fact you belong more to Crvenka than to Sivac?

47
00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:13.900
More, yes, but a cadastral border separates us.

48
00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:14.980
That's what divides us.

49
00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:20.800
Well, and then we started getting together, agreeing, and at first I went alone.

50
00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:22.660
For myself.

51
00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:24.100
And where did you turn? To whom?

52
00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:31.280
In Kula, in Sivac, first in Sivac, then they sent me to Kula, to the Construction Department.

53
00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:34.420
The Construction Department said it has nothing to do with this.

54
00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:36.100
Then to the municipality.

55
00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:40.660
They tossed me around like a ball, whoosh-whoosh, back and forth.

56
00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:47.580
But in essence all that needs to be done is to build a transformer substation, for which you would provide the space.

57
00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:49.160
I would give the space.

58
00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:50.620
Gladly.

59
00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:57.800
Let "Elektrodistribucija" build it, so that we can all get power.

60
00:05:57.800 --> 00:05:58.700
And roughly how much does that cost?

61
00:05:58.880 --> 00:05:59.540
No, I don't know.

62
00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:07.520
One comes, promises, leaves — nothing. Another comes, promises, leaves.

63
00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:11.660
As the authorities changed, so did the promises.

64
00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:15.140
But all those promises went down the drain.

65
00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:16.580
There's nothing.

66
00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:18.380
We don't exist.

67
00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:28.040
Then we decided, partly on the advice of smart people, since we're simple people after all, not that educated.

68
00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:31.960
You walked to school, what are you lacking?

69
00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:33.520
Yes, eight grades.

70
00:06:37.420 --> 00:06:39.140
And you didn't buy, and now some people do buy it.

71
00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.220
I don't buy.

72
00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:46.660
What I have, I have.

73
00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:47.600
What I don't have, I don't need.

74
00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:51.900
And so, my Olena, it came to the point

75
00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:59.160
that one person advised us, who even wrote to Strasbourg about this electricity,

76
00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:02.320
that this is, after all, a violation of human rights.

77
00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:10.880
And they printed this petition for us.

78
00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:17.340
But for this petition to be addressed to Tadić and to be a constitutional petition.

79
00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:21.180
About what we have a right to under the Constitution, under the law.

80
00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:27.420
We all signed, over a hundred people, you have this document.

81
00:07:32.940 --> 00:07:36.600
Yes, yes, yes, everyone — both those who have a weekend house and those who don't.

82
00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:42.160
There were over a hundred of us taxpayers.

83
00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:51.360
Then journalists — there was the director of "Elektrodistribucija" in Sombor,

84
00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:53.700
and they contacted him.

85
00:07:53.960 --> 00:08:02.560
He stated that we — both weekenders and farmstead residents here — are unprofitable for them.

86
00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:05.500
We're unprofitable.

87
00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:06.640
And why?

88
00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:09.040
That he didn't explain.

89
00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:12.700
Because only hotels on Kopaonik are profitable?

90
00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:15.900
No, I don't know, he didn't explain that.

91
00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:23.720
Nowhere in the Constitution did I find that I should live in this country only if I'm profitable to someone.

92
00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:30.400
I'm a citizen of this country, I live here, I pay taxes here, I vote here,

93
00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:33.360
I earn dinars here, and I spend those dinars here.

94
00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:34.400
True.

95
00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:38.820
And if on top of that I have to be profitable to someone,

96
00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:42.280
then let him tell me in what way I'm supposed to be profitable.

97
00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:44.380
How do you charge your mobile phone?

98
00:08:45.740 --> 00:08:48.560
I see you have modern equipment...

99
00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:50.820
Well, I have to have that.

100
00:08:51.580 --> 00:08:59.000
First, to keep up, even though I've been thrown somewhere to the backwoods, into some tenth century.

101
00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:02.640
But I can't accept that, I'm in the 21st century after all.

102
00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:03.080
True.

103
00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:09.960
That is, you basically refused to accept living in the 19th century.

104
00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:11.340
No, no.

105
00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:13.340
And I can't accept it.

106
00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:18.260
In some ways you live in that century, but still you live in the modern world.

107
00:09:18.260 --> 00:09:20.200
I live in that century because

108
00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:24.420
I have two freezers in Sivac, five kilometers from home.

109
00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:27.260
And so, you have to take things there, you have to bring things back.

110
00:09:27.340 --> 00:09:29.840
If you can; and if you can't — more gets thrown out than eaten.

111
00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:30.600
Do you drive?

112
00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:33.440
I drive now with great difficulty.

113
00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:36.640
Still yes, but with great difficulty.

114
00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:39.620
So, in that century I live there.

115
00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:47.900
And in this century I live like this: we have a battery which we take to the village to charge.

116
00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:56.100
Then I bring it home, along with a car charger, and from the car charger I charge the phone.

117
00:10:16.710 --> 00:10:20.800
Because the voltage in this battery isn't always the same.

118
00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:22.790
Sometimes more, sometimes less.

119
00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:25.410
Sometimes it discharges more, sometimes less.

120
00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:34.030
So these chargers get an unstable current,

121
00:10:35.170 --> 00:10:37.490
stronger, weaker, and burn out from it.

122
00:10:38.410 --> 00:10:40.390
So you have to count it like this:

123
00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:42.810
the battery gets charged twice a month.

124
00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:46.950
You have to count one charge a month.

125
00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:52.170
And you have to count the fuel to drive 20 km for this battery.

126
00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:57.370
All of this is expense and very large costs for me.

127
00:10:57.570 --> 00:11:01.030
And besides expenses and costs, it's also very hard,

128
00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:05.990
because I walk with great difficulty, and I have to get in the car and drive to Sivac.

129
00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:08.330
Because it has to be done, there's no one else.

130
00:11:09.010 --> 00:11:11.490
My husband isn't capable of it, he's ill.

131
00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:13.050
It has to be done, there's no one else.

132
00:11:14.030 --> 00:11:16.730
It's a lot and very hard for me.

133
00:12:22.690 --> 00:12:24.550
Finally we arrived in Sivac.

134
00:12:24.770 --> 00:12:26.370
On the way we talked about this.

135
00:12:26.830 --> 00:12:29.090
We arrived at the house of our friends

136
00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:31.170
where the freezers are.

137
00:12:32.370 --> 00:12:34.430
There, this is one, this is the second.

138
00:12:35.030 --> 00:12:36.430
Two freezers.

139
00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:42.640
Unfortunately, like this in the 21st century.

140
00:13:17.960 --> 00:13:20.600
We meet each other halfway, that's true, but...

141
00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:24.780
True, but it would be better if they were at your home.

142
00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:25.460
Well, of course.

143
00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:31.760
You take it out and cook. But this way — when there's fuel to come, then you cook.

144
00:13:35.260 --> 00:13:37.100
Then you cook, no other way.

145
00:13:42.060 --> 00:13:45.940
Maybe God will look upon the poor too.

146
00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:33.440
We go out, the same system as there.

147
00:14:34.860 --> 00:14:36.460
Because I can't do it any other way.

148
00:16:06.990 --> 00:16:08.090
Well, enjoy your meal.

149
00:16:09.290 --> 00:16:10.490
Eat, eat.

150
00:16:13.270 --> 00:16:14.450
Good dinner.

151
00:16:16.050 --> 00:16:18.690
What's this, you put two little pieces on your plate,

152
00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:22.490
so as not to eat but to get to the pancakes sooner, right?

153
00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:23.670
No.

154
00:16:24.470 --> 00:16:27.530
You won't get to the pancakes until you've had your fill of beans.

155
00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:28.070
I won't allow it.

156
00:16:31.350 --> 00:16:33.590
Depends on the capacity of the stomach.

157
00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:03.240
We haven't cooked them for a month now.

158
00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:07.840
You know what?

159
00:17:25.920 --> 00:17:27.300
Never mind. You have everything.

160
00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:30.600
Both milk and eggs and flour.

161
00:17:31.460 --> 00:17:37.250
Winter season, no work, snow on the ground.

162
00:17:42.670 --> 00:17:44.050
Nowhere to go.

163
00:17:51.690 --> 00:17:52.790
Some feed the cows,

164
00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:55.010
clean the barn,

165
00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:01.120
carry straw,

166
00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:04.340
someone husks corn.

167
00:18:04.420 --> 00:18:05.740
And Danilo is playing the cook?

168
00:18:05.740 --> 00:18:07.540
And I'm playing the cook.

169
00:18:26.630 --> 00:18:27.730
It's warm in the room.

170
00:18:31.970 --> 00:18:34.490
And before that they drank rakija.

171
00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:41.440
I won't praise you too much,

172
00:18:41.660 --> 00:18:42.900
nor scold you.

173
00:18:45.370 --> 00:18:48.990
I'll say just one thing: everyone would like

174
00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:53.550
to have such a cook and such a wife.

175
00:18:53.550 --> 00:19:13.100
Have you ever gone anywhere from this farmstead?

176
00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:13.920
No.

177
00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:15.080
Gone?

178
00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:17.180
I did, but not...

179
00:19:17.510 --> 00:19:19.560
I don't mean to live,

180
00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:21.360
but did you travel anywhere?

181
00:19:22.900 --> 00:19:25.600
I went to various events while I could.

182
00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:27.320
What events?

183
00:19:27.320 --> 00:19:33.880
Here, on the farmstead, a great many events took place.

184
00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:41.220
I was that crazy woman who ran from entrepreneur to entrepreneur,

185
00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:45.620
from company to company and collected sponsorship money to hold a harvest the old way,

186
00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:48.560
to hold an old-fashioned corn harvest,

187
00:19:49.100 --> 00:19:55.620
to hold a review of folklore, handicrafts, folk costumes, everything else.

188
00:19:55.620 --> 00:19:57.400
While I had the strength.

189
00:19:58.400 --> 00:20:01.500
I got no help, because no one was interested,

190
00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:04.500
although it's an ethno-farmstead, it's registered as such.

191
00:20:04.520 --> 00:20:06.120
And when did you register this farmstead?

192
00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:11.400
This farmstead is registered as an ethno-farmstead,

193
00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:14.500
registered as a tourist destination

194
00:20:14.500 --> 00:20:18.020
and registered for practicing old customs, which is what we did.

195
00:20:18.040 --> 00:20:19.340
Since when?

196
00:20:21.100 --> 00:20:22.140
For 12 years now.

197
00:22:09.370 --> 00:22:14.930
When the laundry is white, you first boil it, then wash it, then rinse it like this.

198
00:22:15.310 --> 00:22:18.250
In winter they wash only if the weather is good.

199
00:22:18.590 --> 00:22:21.790
If the weather is bad — they wash one item at a time,

200
00:22:21.890 --> 00:22:26.330
and rinse in the house, if Danilo has the strength

201
00:22:26.330 --> 00:22:28.850
to carry the water in and out.

202
00:22:28.850 --> 00:22:56.310
Life here, in the 21st century, 180 meters from electricity.

203
00:23:01.600 --> 00:23:03.760
For me it's not only this government that's to blame.

204
00:23:04.540 --> 00:23:06.540
Every government,

205
00:23:06.760 --> 00:23:09.040
some 25 years ago,

206
00:23:09.100 --> 00:23:10.940
with a full set of documents,

207
00:23:10.940 --> 00:23:15.240
I pestered every government, and every one stayed deaf.

208
00:23:15.620 --> 00:23:20.240
So all of them can go in one barrel and to hell,

209
00:23:20.280 --> 00:23:21.720
into the Black Sea down the Danube.

210
00:23:21.840 --> 00:23:23.780
That they're all the same.

211
00:23:24.020 --> 00:23:27.920
It's pure proof that toward the people no one ever,

212
00:23:27.920 --> 00:23:29.440
no government had any sympathy.

213
00:23:30.220 --> 00:23:35.580
As for electricity, I, a one-hundred-percent invalid,

214
00:23:36.660 --> 00:23:39.120
and my husband, who is ill —

215
00:23:39.880 --> 00:23:44.100
you can imagine what electricity would mean for two such people.

216
00:23:44.340 --> 00:23:47.580
For me to have a light bulb, to have somewhere to wash,

217
00:23:48.060 --> 00:23:50.200
to have somewhere to put a freezer,

218
00:23:50.300 --> 00:23:54.480
I have a freezer in the village, five kilometers from home.

219
00:23:54.760 --> 00:23:57.660
Nobody wants illness, nobody wants misfortune.

220
00:23:57.660 --> 00:23:59.900
And misfortune is just what found me.

221
00:24:00.420 --> 00:24:06.900
That I, like this, should be rinsing laundry outdoors in the month of February.

222
00:24:09.480 --> 00:24:18.440
In Montenegro, in Serbia, in Bosnia, Switzerland —

223
00:24:18.440 --> 00:24:21.520
and on top of that hill over there a light bulb is burning.

224
00:24:21.820 --> 00:24:26.360
In flat Vojvodina, where a machine can in 15–20 minutes

225
00:24:26.360 --> 00:24:30.240
dig up to my farmstead to lay an underground cable —

226
00:24:30.240 --> 00:24:31.160
there's no electricity.

227
00:24:31.860 --> 00:24:33.100
Isn't that a disgrace?

228
00:24:33.920 --> 00:24:34.820
Where am I to go?

229
00:24:36.240 --> 00:24:37.280
Only to the cemetery.

230
00:24:38.960 --> 00:24:41.140
And I won't go there either, they'll carry me there.

231
00:24:43.110 --> 00:24:43.810
Sad.

232
00:24:45.410 --> 00:24:48.890
But I'm not surprised it is so.

233
00:24:48.970 --> 00:24:49.830
This is my trouble.

234
00:24:50.650 --> 00:24:53.310
And to each their own trouble hurts the most.

235
00:24:53.930 --> 00:24:56.730
And nobody heals another's wound.

236
00:24:57.230 --> 00:24:58.830
Everyone heals their own.

237
00:24:58.830 --> 00:25:01.870
And I heal mine as best I can.

238
00:25:02.170 --> 00:25:06.850
People come and say: oh, how good you have it here on the farmstead.

239
00:25:09.750 --> 00:25:10.750
And I think to myself:

240
00:25:11.210 --> 00:25:15.110
ah, if you'd suffered what I have, you'd never say it's good.

241
00:25:15.970 --> 00:25:17.110
It's good for me

242
00:25:17.170 --> 00:25:19.890
because it's the house I was born in and live in.

243
00:25:20.470 --> 00:25:21.450
It's good for me.

244
00:25:21.510 --> 00:25:22.590
That's why it's good.

245
00:25:22.870 --> 00:25:25.690
And everything else is foul and black torment.

246
00:25:40.720 --> 00:25:42.760
and we'll agree to get this solved.

247
00:25:42.900 --> 00:25:45.820
This is no big problem.